# PY/captures/
DadaGP-v1.1/
# Shared scraper→decoder→enricher output (populated at runtime; lives on the
# 6 TB data drive). Nothing under output/ is committed — git holds code and the
# manifest only; durability of scraped data comes from the external-drive
# backup (scripts/maintain.sh), not from git.
/output/
# Other large derived/data trees (same policy: local disk + backup where
# irreplaceable, never git).
/renders/
/dataset/
# The committed manifest is an explicit allowlist: ignore everything under
# manifest/ (Phase 2's per-tab alignment warps, Phase 1's requests/, etc. are
# derived and can grow huge), then re-include exactly the snapshot files. Never
# `git add manifest/`. See plans/phase_0.md "Git-commit boundary".
/manifest/**
!/manifest/manifest.jsonl
!/manifest/overrides.json
!/manifest/report.md
